  "summary": "All 8 results inbox items worked per RBC-INBOX-01 and closed. Each patient was confirmed by two identifiers before anything was written to the chart.\n\n1. Raj Patel (pt-0006), FIT positive: an active GI colonoscopy referral already existed (sr-t2-gi-1020), so it was linked and no duplicate placed (RBC-GI-01 §2). Patient messaged; note written.\n2. Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), renal ultrasound: simple cyst, report says no follow-up needed. Closed with a comment that no follow-up is needed under RBC-INBOX-01 §3.\n3–4. Edra Ondricka (pt-0016), TSH and lipid panel: both normal. Acknowledged and closed.\n5. Linda Marsh (pt-0013), outside CT abdomen/pelvis (St. Brigid ED, 2026-06-04): the 5 mm right lower lobe lung nodule was already being followed in lung cancer screening (Lung-RADS 2 on 2025-09-15). Her annual screening CT (LDCT) was due 2026-09-15 and its ±1-month window has passed. Under RBC-RAD-05 §2, ordered the screening LDCT (sr-t0007) for 2026-10-23 to 2026-11-06, with a tracking task due 2026-11-06 (task-t0008). Patient messaged; note written.\n6. Tomás Ruiz (pt-0053, age 16), right knee X-ray: aggressive lytic lesion of the lower femur, suspected primary bone tumour. Under RBC-RAD-05 §3, ordered an urgent MRI femur with and without contrast (sr-t0012) and an urgent orthopaedic oncology referral (sr-t0013), both for 2026-10-23 to 2026-11-05. Tracking tasks are due 2026-11-05 (task-t0015, task-t0016). Created an urgent task for Jordan Reyes NP to call his mother Ana Ruiz today (task-t0014). Also sent an urgent portal message with activity restrictions and when to seek care. Note written.\n7. Walter Brennan (pt-0008), potassium 6.4, sample hemolyzed: under RBC-LAB-03 §2, ordered an urgent repeat BMP for no later than Monday 2026-10-26 (sr-t0025) and messaged him to come in. On-call was not notified, per policy. Note written.\n8. Denise Holloway (pt-0010), potassium 6.2, not hemolyzed, creatinine 1.58: under RBC-LAB-03 §1, ordered a stat BMP (sr-t0020)